          "kicker": "World Cup selection",
          "heading": "Borthwick rings 10 changes for Japan, telling hopefuls to put team first",
          "body": "England head coach Steve Borthwick has made 10 personnel and two positional changes for Saturday's Nations Championship match against Japan, handing starts to Will Joseph and Max Ojomoh. Borthwick says he is \"really aware that the narrative around World Cup selection exists\", but he insists the team must come first. Hopefuls have been warned not to go off script, with Henry Pollock starting at No 8 for a second time and only three players keeping their positions from the Australia win."
        },
