    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-13",
      "edition": "Friday 13 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Beirne captains Ireland as Farrell names seven changes for Fiji",
          "body": "Tadhg Beirne captains Ireland at the Aviva Stadium for the first time as Andy Farrell names seven changes for Saturday's Nations Championship match against Fiji. Beirne takes over from Dan Sheehan, who is out with concussion, while Mack Hansen moves to full-back and Jamison Gibson-Park returns to scrum-half after coming off the bench against Argentina. Ulster's James McNabney is named among the replacements and is in line to make his debut, and Nick Timoney shifts to number eight amid injuries to Caelan Doris, Jack Conan and Sean Jansen."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
