      "date": "2026-11-13",
      "edition": "Friday 13 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Quesada names five changes to face Argentina, with Varney starting at scrum-half",
          "body": "Head coach Gonzalo Quesada made five changes after the 7-66 defeat to South Africa: Allan moves to fullback, Varney starts at scrum-half and Fischetti returns at prop. The coach said some players arrived at camp not ready for 80 minutes, either after too much game time, as with Vintcent and Varney, or too little, as with Zuliani, so he picked a balanced side able to keep the pace. Argentina are missing Montoya, so Bautista Bernasconi starts at hooker, and Quesada expects the Pumas to come out aggressive from the first minute."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wallabies prop Angus Bell sin-binned for hip drop tackle",
