      "edition": "Friday 13 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Taine Basham starts at No. 8 as Aaron Wainwright is ruled out",
          "body": "Aaron Wainwright picked up the minor calf injury against Japan and spent the week in a protective boot before being ruled out of Saturday's test against New Zealand. Taine Basham, recalled after impressing for Cardiff, replaces him, his first Test since the 2024 Six Nations. Wales head coach Steve Tandy said: \"I'm delighted that Taine gets an opportunity this weekend.\" James Botham starts at blindside in place of Alex Mann, and Adam Beard returns to the second row."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
