      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline call",
          "heading": "Wallabies prop Angus Bell becomes first yellow-carded for hip drop tackle",
          "body": "Wallabies prop Angus Bell was sin-binned after a television match official review on the first weekend of the Nations Championship. World Rugby formally outlawed the hip drop tackle on 1 November, so this window is the first in which referees have been asked to clamp down on it. Bell's tackle left England wing Immanuel Feyi-Waboso with an ankle injury that has ruled him out of England's remaining Nations Championship campaign. Australia's next assignment is Scotland at Murrayfield on Sunday."
        },
